1108
01:22:33,920 --> 01:22:39,040
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: That I spoke about to Senior Associate Justice Marvic Leonen.

1109
01:22:39,180 --> 01:22:40,980
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I told him about this problem that we have.

1110
01:22:41,780 --> 01:22:48,460
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Because institutionally, it's very discouraging to be conducting all of these activities

1111
01:22:48,460 --> 01:22:56,020
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: only to be reversed by the Court of Appeals decision that came out of nowhere.

1112
01:22:56,180 --> 01:22:57,880
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I mean, sometimes we feel that way.

1113
01:22:58,620 --> 01:23:03,120
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And I was actually confronted with that problem as Secretary of Justice

1114
01:23:03,120 --> 01:23:03,520
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: because...

1115
01:23:03,920 --> 01:23:07,320
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: There was somebody dismissed by the office of the ombudsman

1116
01:23:07,320 --> 01:23:10,280
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: who was...

1117
01:23:10,280 --> 01:23:12,440
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Which decision was reversed by the Court of Appeals

1118
01:23:12,440 --> 01:23:17,960
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: and was trying to get back to his office in the NBI.

1119
01:23:19,100 --> 01:23:23,300
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And I could not honor that kind of logic

1120
01:23:23,300 --> 01:23:24,980
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: because he had been dismissed already.

1121
01:23:25,760 --> 01:23:30,000
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And if you will be reversed in your dismissal,

1122
01:23:30,480 --> 01:23:32,100
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: what then is the power given to us?

1123
01:23:32,100 --> 01:23:33,520
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: If that will be the case.

1124
01:23:33,920 --> 01:23:37,400
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: So, that's one of the dilemmas that we face with the judiciary, Your Honor.

1125
01:23:37,800 --> 01:23:39,980
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I'm sorry to say, but as a lawyer,

1126
01:23:40,340 --> 01:23:45,000
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: it's not really common for lawyers to complain about the courts.

1127
01:23:45,660 --> 01:23:48,060
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But sometimes we just have to raise that issue already

1128
01:23:48,060 --> 01:23:53,040
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: because it can be the biggest elephant in the room within our justice system.

1129
01:23:53,420 --> 01:23:55,520
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: If you talk about foreign investment,

1130
01:23:56,160 --> 01:23:58,620
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: we have a problem with foreign investment

1131
01:23:58,620 --> 01:24:03,560
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: because there's no certainty that the rules will apply to the judiciary.

1132
01:24:03,920 --> 01:24:07,960
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It's something that has to be dealt with face-to-face by our people

1133
01:24:07,960 --> 01:24:11,540
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: and by the legislators, by all of us.

1134
01:24:12,140 --> 01:24:14,880
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It's the biggest elephant in the room for this country.

1135
01:24:15,640 --> 01:24:20,360
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: The judiciary has to be examined closely by everybody in government

1136
01:24:20,360 --> 01:24:22,920
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: and they themselves should go on a soul-searching

1137
01:24:22,920 --> 01:24:25,000
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: so that we can be a better country.

1138
01:24:25,220 --> 01:24:27,580
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I think that that's one of the problems besetting us right now.

1139
01:24:29,770 --> 01:24:32,990
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Ombudsman, I really appreciate your...

1140
01:24:35,330 --> 01:24:39,390
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: being proactive instead of just waiting for cases to be filed

1141
01:24:39,390 --> 01:24:40,510
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: and aaktuhan.

1142
01:24:40,950 --> 01:24:43,350
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Yung nakikita ko na proactive ngayon ang Ombudsman,

1143
01:24:43,410 --> 01:24:48,930
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: meaning you go after the issues before it explodes,

1144
01:24:49,110 --> 01:24:50,990
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: which is the right way to do.

1145
01:24:51,670 --> 01:24:55,030
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: However, kagaya ng nasabi ng ating mga kasamahan,

1146
01:24:55,250 --> 01:24:58,610
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: the wheels of justice, kasama dito ang judiciary.

1147
01:24:59,490 --> 01:25:03,790
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Kanina narinig ko sinabi niyo na it takes on average 15 years in the Sandiganbayan

1148
01:25:03,790 --> 01:25:05,310
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: to resolve a case.

1149
01:25:05,330 --> 01:25:12,050
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Ngayon, the CA also reverses a lot of the decisions you make.

1150
01:25:12,990 --> 01:25:14,850
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And I'm not blaming them.

1151
01:25:15,170 --> 01:25:20,030
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I am just saying, yung wheels of justice putol eh.

1152
01:25:20,230 --> 01:25:21,310
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Hindi gumugulong eh.

1153
01:25:21,510 --> 01:25:22,410
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Parang na-stuck up siya.

1154
01:25:23,010 --> 01:25:28,670
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So what efforts is the ombudsman doing together with the judiciary

1155
01:25:28,670 --> 01:25:34,670
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: to resolve this turning of the will of justice

1156
01:25:34,670 --> 01:25:35,310
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: to make it more effective?

1157
01:25:35,330 --> 01:25:41,810
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: More efficient, faster, and also to make it just for our constituents?

1158
01:25:42,110 --> 01:25:44,210
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Kasi kung ang Ombudsman proactive,

1159
01:25:44,870 --> 01:25:45,830
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: kabilang banda naman hindi,

1160
01:25:46,830 --> 01:25:48,550
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: sayang, sayang yung efforts.

1161
01:25:49,270 --> 01:25:55,430
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Well, that's something that I looked at when I was Secretary of Justice, Your Honor.

1162
01:25:56,130 --> 01:25:57,830
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: When I was the Secretary of Justice,

1163
01:25:57,970 --> 01:26:00,910
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: we had this Justice Sector Coordinating Council,

1164
01:26:00,910 --> 01:26:04,630
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: which involved the courts, the Department of Justice,

1165
01:26:05,330 --> 01:26:07,650
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: and the Department of Interior and Local Government

1166
01:26:07,650 --> 01:26:09,990
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: so that we could coordinate our efforts.

1167
01:26:10,890 --> 01:26:15,470
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But actually, that was a program sponsored by the European Union.

1168
01:26:15,810 --> 01:26:17,810
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: They were the ones that funded that program.

1169
01:26:18,470 --> 01:26:22,030
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Probably, we need one that will include the ombudsman, Your Honor,

1170
01:26:22,630 --> 01:26:25,010
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: so that the wills of justice will grind faster.

1171
01:26:25,810 --> 01:26:29,850
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And if you ask me, I mean, if we look back in history,

1172
01:26:29,850 --> 01:26:33,750
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I think I was in law school when EDSA happened.

1173
01:26:33,750 --> 01:26:36,410
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And if there's one thing that was never touched

1174
01:26:36,410 --> 01:26:40,850
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: with all the EDSAs that happened to this country,

1175
01:26:41,210 --> 01:26:41,970
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: it's the judiciary.

1176
01:26:42,990 --> 01:26:48,470
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Never has the judiciary accounted for everything that they've been doing.

1177
01:26:49,210 --> 01:26:51,550
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It is something that we have to examine as a country.

1178
01:26:52,150 --> 01:26:59,510
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Because when businessmen come in to invest and create jobs

1179
01:26:59,510 --> 01:27:01,750
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: and give progress to the country,

1180
01:27:02,190 --> 01:27:03,710
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: when a case is thrown,

1181
01:27:03,750 --> 01:27:06,410
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: and a monkey wrench is thrown into the business,

1182
01:27:06,710 --> 01:27:09,850
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: there's no certainty that the case will be finished

1183
01:27:09,850 --> 01:27:11,210
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: within a certain amount of time.

1184
01:27:11,770 --> 01:27:15,090
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It is something that has to be addressed also by our people,

1185
01:27:15,310 --> 01:27:17,730
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: by the senior members of the Supreme Court

1186
01:27:17,730 --> 01:27:21,570
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: about how fast can justice roll, the wills of justice roll.

1187
01:27:22,370 --> 01:27:27,430
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It's actually a problem that has been there for the longest time.

1188
01:27:27,950 --> 01:27:30,210
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But it has to be said openly.

1189
01:27:30,490 --> 01:27:32,110
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I'm daring to do this, Your Honor,

1190
01:27:32,110 --> 01:27:33,650
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: because I have no more.

1191
01:27:33,750 --> 01:27:34,150
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I have no more aspirations.

1192
01:27:34,450 --> 01:27:38,990
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: This is the job I want for myself and for the country

1193
01:27:38,990 --> 01:27:41,050
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: to be able to finish this job, Your Honor.

1194
01:27:41,730 --> 01:27:45,210
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And that's why things that have been left unsaid

1195
01:27:45,210 --> 01:27:48,170
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: are being said now because it has to happen.

1196
01:27:48,630 --> 01:27:51,770
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: If we're able to cure our justice system

1197
01:27:51,770 --> 01:27:53,330
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: and make it function properly,

1198
01:27:53,750 --> 01:27:55,590
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: we will be a much better country, Your Honor.

1199
01:27:55,770 --> 01:27:57,530
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: We will be a much, much better country.

1200
01:27:58,670 --> 01:28:01,190
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: With your coordination, what's the feedback?

1201
01:28:01,190 --> 01:28:02,650
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I heard you say na meron

1202
01:28:02,650 --> 01:28:03,190
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: you have a...

1203
01:28:03,750 --> 01:28:05,750
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Coordination or that committee.

1204
01:28:06,430 --> 01:28:08,030
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Now, what's the feedback from the judiciary?

1205
01:28:08,430 --> 01:28:08,770
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Are they all...

1206
01:28:08,770 --> 01:28:11,110
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Well, I usually speak to my classmates.

1207
01:28:11,210 --> 01:28:12,430
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I usually speak to my classmates,

1208
01:28:12,790 --> 01:28:14,910
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Senior Associate Justice Marvic Leonen.

1209
01:28:15,470 --> 01:28:18,190
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Of course, sometimes he questions me about speaking out

1210
01:28:18,190 --> 01:28:20,090
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: about these things that I'm saying.

1211
01:28:20,710 --> 01:28:21,730
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But it has to be said.

1212
01:28:22,410 --> 01:28:23,790
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: We cannot hold this back anymore.

1213
01:28:24,010 --> 01:28:27,930
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I mean, how many times do you have in your life

1214
01:28:27,930 --> 01:28:28,990
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: to serve as ombudsman

1215
01:28:28,990 --> 01:28:32,930
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: and give your critique of what's happening in society?

1216
01:28:33,050 --> 01:28:33,630
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Because it is a role...

1217
01:28:33,630 --> 01:28:34,790
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It is a role that was given to us.

1218
01:28:36,030 --> 01:28:39,150
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It's something that probably I may be cautioned,

1219
01:28:39,190 --> 01:28:40,930
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: but the message arrives.

1220
01:28:41,570 --> 01:28:46,130
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And I'm sure that I have distressed our Chief Justice

1221
01:28:46,130 --> 01:28:47,770
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: many times with my remarks.

1222
01:28:48,330 --> 01:28:49,330
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But it has to happen.

1223
01:28:49,470 --> 01:28:50,710
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It has to be done, Your Honor.

1224
01:28:51,070 --> 01:28:53,830
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I'm doing this at great risk probably to many lawyers.

1225
01:28:54,370 --> 01:28:57,370
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: They will not even think about doing something like this.

1226
01:28:57,710 --> 01:28:59,710
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But I think I've arrived at the point

1227
01:28:59,710 --> 01:29:02,730
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: where this has to be said properly, Your Honor,

1228
01:29:02,750 --> 01:29:03,450
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: in order to make it happen.

1229
01:29:03,450 --> 01:29:04,950
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: In open court, in open session,

1230
01:29:05,810 --> 01:29:10,550
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: so that people will know what ails us

1231
01:29:10,550 --> 01:29:12,770
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: and that there is a light at the end of the tunnel

1232
01:29:12,770 --> 01:29:14,110
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: if we really look at it.

1233
01:29:14,690 --> 01:29:16,070
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And that is one of them, Your Honor,

1234
01:29:16,190 --> 01:29:17,730
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: is to be able to correct

1235
01:29:17,730 --> 01:29:21,570
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: and then make efficient the wheels of justice, Your Honor.

1236
01:29:23,130 --> 01:29:24,870
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I support that, Ombudsman.

1237
01:29:25,170 --> 01:29:31,670
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And like mga ano lang, in the ordinary day-to-day activities

1238
01:29:32,350 --> 01:29:33,050
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: of our country,

1239
01:29:33,450 --> 01:29:33,950
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: our constituents,

1240
01:29:34,770 --> 01:29:36,670
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: especially in public service,

1241
01:29:38,010 --> 01:29:39,850
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: kagaya po sa mga kapitan,

1242
01:29:40,590 --> 01:29:42,090
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: iyan diretso sa tao iyan.

1243
01:29:42,830 --> 01:29:45,570
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And pag nagsumbong ang tao sa Ombudsman

1244
01:29:45,570 --> 01:29:48,070
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: or sa ibang mga government agencies,

1245
01:29:48,190 --> 01:29:50,970
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: kung hindi nag-function yung accountability mechanism natin,

1246
01:29:51,610 --> 01:29:55,230
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: when I say accountability, lahat ito,

1247
01:29:55,410 --> 01:29:57,450
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: from the Ombudsman to the judiciary,

1248
01:29:58,910 --> 01:29:59,450
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: hindi naman

1249
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:03,940
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: nadedehado yung respondent

1250
01:30:03,940 --> 01:30:05,180
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: o yung nakusahan.

1251
01:30:05,180 --> 01:30:07,140
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Nadedehado yung taong bayan.

1252
01:30:07,540 --> 01:30:09,100
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Sila ang nadedehado dito.

1253
01:30:09,680 --> 01:30:11,260
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Kaya I really support

1254
01:30:11,260 --> 01:30:13,620
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: making our

1255
01:30:13,620 --> 01:30:14,940
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: wills of justice efficient.

1256
01:30:15,220 --> 01:30:17,340
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And that's what hopefully we can

1257
01:30:17,340 --> 01:30:19,360
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: contribute

1258
01:30:19,360 --> 01:30:21,040
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: during the budget season.

1259
01:30:21,460 --> 01:30:23,420
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: In all aspects, in all agencies

1260
01:30:23,420 --> 01:30:23,980
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: as well.

1261
01:30:25,080 --> 01:30:26,020
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Thank you, Your Honor.

1262
01:30:26,420 --> 01:30:29,180
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I have a few items in the budget

