Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: feedback.

1292
01:31:28,960 --> 01:31:30,800
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: On why this program increased

1293
01:31:30,800 --> 01:31:32,800
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: by almost three-folds.

1294
01:31:33,300 --> 01:31:35,660
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Your Honor, in the Ombudsman's office,

1295
01:31:35,660 --> 01:31:36,860
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: we have a small auditorium

1296
01:31:37,540 --> 01:31:38,980
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: where we entertain

1297
01:31:39,900 --> 01:31:42,000
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: students and advocates

1298
01:31:42,000 --> 01:31:43,200
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: of good governance

1299
01:31:43,840 --> 01:31:45,940
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: to give us a visit so that we can

1300
01:31:45,940 --> 01:31:47,580
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: have a dialogue and they can observe

1301
01:31:48,100 --> 01:31:49,620
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: the goings-on in our office.

1302
01:31:50,220 --> 01:31:52,540
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And we deem this to be a very effective

1303
01:31:52,540 --> 01:31:53,940
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: tool, Your Honor, especially

1304
01:31:54,400 --> 01:31:56,100
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: with young people being brought in.

1305
01:31:57,100 --> 01:31:58,960
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: People who are in high

1306
01:31:58,960 --> 01:32:02,300
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: school, whose minds

1307
01:32:02,300 --> 01:32:05,140
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: who are in their formative years,

1308
01:32:05,140 --> 01:32:07,200
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: can be able to absorb the ideas

1309
01:32:07,200 --> 01:32:10,660
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: of fighting corruption very early.

1310
01:32:10,660 --> 01:32:12,940
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It has to start, I mean,

1311
01:32:12,940 --> 01:32:14,940
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Your Honor, if we can do this as a program

1312
01:32:14,940 --> 01:32:17,580
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: in our educational system,

1313
01:32:17,580 --> 01:32:20,980
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I think we would really be a better country.

1314
01:32:20,980 --> 01:32:23,440
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It's something that has to start from the youth.

1315
01:32:23,440 --> 01:32:27,580
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It's like when we marvel at the Japanese children

1316
01:32:27,580 --> 01:32:28,960
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: walking to school,

1317
01:32:28,960 --> 01:32:33,040
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: unaccompanied by parents without any assistance,

1318
01:32:33,040 --> 01:32:35,500
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: because the culture has been created to do that.

1319
01:32:35,500 --> 01:32:37,740
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It's something that we can create in our country

1320
01:32:37,740 --> 01:32:42,900
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: to start them young in trying to fight corruption

1321
01:32:42,900 --> 01:32:45,780
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: and to be able to know the concept of corruption

1322
01:32:45,780 --> 01:32:47,680
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: as a bad concept, Your Honor.

1323
01:32:48,940 --> 01:32:50,980
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Thank you for that, Ombudsman.

1324
01:32:50,980 --> 01:32:52,540
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I really support that.

1325
01:32:52,540 --> 01:32:56,040
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: If we can open the eyes and minds of our students

1326
01:32:56,040 --> 01:32:58,840
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: in not being in integrity,

1327
01:32:58,960 --> 01:32:59,960
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: and fighting corruption,

1328
01:32:59,960 --> 01:33:04,080
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I think that is the best direction.

1329
01:33:04,080 --> 01:33:09,280
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And is this program directed towards that?

1330
01:33:09,280 --> 01:33:11,080
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Yung mga sa mga bata?

1331
01:33:11,080 --> 01:33:14,200
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Yes, Your Honor.

1332
01:33:14,200 --> 01:33:16,200
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Actually, meron akong anecdote.

1333
01:33:16,200 --> 01:33:17,960
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Nakwento ko ito sa ating chairman eh.

1334
01:33:17,960 --> 01:33:21,600
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Pag may mga lumalapit sa akin

1335
01:33:21,600 --> 01:33:25,240
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: humihingi ng job recommendation sa gobyerno,

1336
01:33:25,240 --> 01:33:28,080
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: ang pinipili nila kaagad customs.

1337
01:33:28,080 --> 01:33:28,880
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: No.

1338
01:33:28,880 --> 01:33:29,440
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Halos lahat.

1339
01:33:29,440 --> 01:33:30,080
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Sabi ko sa inyo, halos lahat

1340
01:33:30,080 --> 01:33:34,120
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: ng recommendation customs.

1341
01:33:34,120 --> 01:33:36,400
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: But the recommendation is for the wrong reason.

1342
01:33:36,400 --> 01:33:42,360
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And I made that example because itong mga batang ito na naghahanap ng trabaho,

1343
01:33:42,360 --> 01:33:44,160
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: wrong reasons yung kanilang iniisip.

1344
01:33:44,160 --> 01:33:45,000
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Bakit customs?

1345
01:33:45,000 --> 01:33:51,200
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Bakit hindi sa DOST or sa ibang mga agencies?

1346
01:33:51,200 --> 01:33:58,080
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So that's why mas maganda kung maaga pa lang eh natuturuan na natin sila.

1347
01:33:58,080 --> 01:33:59,360
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Yung kultura nila maiba,

1348
01:33:59,360 --> 01:34:01,400
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: yung kanilang pag-iisip.

1349
01:34:01,400 --> 01:34:04,040
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Your Honor, I also encountered the same.

1350
01:34:04,040 --> 01:34:10,120
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I had the same experience as somebody working for government.

1351
01:34:10,120 --> 01:34:14,920
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Not only customs, but immigration is another target for many of them.

1352
01:34:14,920 --> 01:34:17,560
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: LTO is another target for many of them.

1353
01:34:17,560 --> 01:34:20,760
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: The revenue-generating agencies actually attract a lot of...

1354
01:34:20,760 --> 01:34:22,360
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And BIR, Your Honor.

1355
01:34:22,360 --> 01:34:23,400
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: The BIR.

1356
01:34:23,400 --> 01:34:25,760
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It's...

1357
01:34:25,760 --> 01:34:27,400
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But we know that it's possible

1358
01:34:27,400 --> 01:34:28,200
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: to change the

1359
01:34:28,200 --> 01:34:29,320
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: culture.

1360
01:34:29,360 --> 01:34:30,520
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Your Honor.

1361
01:34:30,520 --> 01:34:35,400
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I think that we have succeeded to a certain extent in the Bureau of Immigration.

1362
01:34:35,400 --> 01:34:38,640
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I think we were able to improve it when I was Secretary of Justice.

1363
01:34:38,640 --> 01:34:41,680
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: The way that it's run, the way that people behave themselves,

1364
01:34:41,680 --> 01:34:43,520
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: the way that they comport themselves.

1365
01:34:43,520 --> 01:34:46,600
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I think it can be done with the proper leadership, Your Honor.

1366
01:34:46,600 --> 01:34:47,640
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Thank you, Mr. Ambudsman.

1367
01:34:47,640 --> 01:34:48,960
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

1368
01:34:48,960 --> 01:34:50,600
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: That's it for me.

1369
01:34:50,600 --> 01:34:51,480
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you.

1370
01:34:51,480 --> 01:34:55,000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Siguro we just have a few questions.

1371
01:34:55,000 --> 01:34:55,880
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Senator Lacson.

1372
01:34:55,880 --> 01:34:56,200
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yes.

1373
01:34:56,200 --> 01:34:57,480
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Gusto ko lang makuha yung official

1374
01:34:57,480 --> 01:34:58,480
Senator Panfilo Lacson: position ng Ombudsman doon sa...

1375
01:34:58,480 --> 01:34:59,200
Senator Panfilo Lacson: kasi nag-pass kami ng

1376
01:34:59,200 --> 01:35:00,400
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Judiciary Fiscal Autonomy Act.

1377
01:35:00,400 --> 01:35:05,080
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Because we passed the Judiciary Fiscal Autonomy Act.

1378
01:35:05,080 --> 01:35:09,160
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Of course, guaranteed naman talaga sa Constitution yung fiscal autonomy.

1379
01:35:09,160 --> 01:35:11,200
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Pero ito na-strengthen pa.

1380
01:35:11,200 --> 01:35:16,080
Senator Panfilo Lacson: But again, ano yung official position ninyo if we enact a similar law

1381
01:35:16,080 --> 01:35:24,390
Senator Panfilo Lacson: that mirrors the statutory powers, yung fiscal autonomy ng judiciary?

1382
01:35:24,390 --> 01:35:28,630
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Your Honor, we have to...

1383
01:35:28,630 --> 01:35:29,950
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I'm in favor of that, Your Honor.

1384
01:35:29,950 --> 01:35:30,470
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: That the judiciary should

1385
01:35:30,470 --> 01:35:30,870
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: have fiscal autonomy.

1386
01:35:30,870 --> 01:35:32,510
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Before that happens,

1387
01:35:32,510 --> 01:35:37,990
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But before that happens, we have to be able to ask them the tough questions

1388
01:35:37,990 --> 01:35:40,350
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: that have to be answered, Your Honor.

1389
01:35:40,350 --> 01:35:47,630
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Because if we isolate the judiciary to the point where they become so independent,

1390
01:35:47,630 --> 01:35:51,350
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: we might be disappointed.

1391
01:35:51,350 --> 01:35:55,430
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: We just want things to be right when we start this, Your Honor.

1392
01:35:55,430 --> 01:35:58,590
Senator Panfilo Lacson: I was referring to the Ombudsman getting the same statutory protection.

1393
01:35:58,590 --> 01:35:59,790
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Magkaroon din kayo,

1394
01:35:59,790 --> 01:36:00,430
Senator Panfilo Lacson: kasi pagka merong fiscal autonomy,

1395
01:36:00,470 --> 01:36:08,990
Senator Panfilo Lacson: yung parang full fiscal autonomy, not just in the implementation,

1396
01:36:08,990 --> 01:36:11,450
Senator Panfilo Lacson: but in the proposal.

1397
01:36:11,450 --> 01:36:17,350
Senator Panfilo Lacson: But I notice also, kasi in spite of the passage of that law,

1398
01:36:17,350 --> 01:36:23,190
Senator Panfilo Lacson: na binibigyan na ng complete fiscal autonomy ang judiciary, nabawasan pa rin sila sa NEP eh.

1399
01:36:23,190 --> 01:36:26,630
Senator Panfilo Lacson: What they proposed. That's why that is an issue that I'd like to raise.

1400
01:36:26,630 --> 01:36:34,490
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Hindi ko lang ni-raise sa DBCC, Mr. President, na bakit nagpasa tayo ng law, may fiscal autonomy,

1401
01:36:34,490 --> 01:36:41,010
Senator Panfilo Lacson: meaning sila na yung nagpe-prepare ng kanilang NEP, at bahala na yung Congress

1402
01:36:41,010 --> 01:36:48,530
Senator Panfilo Lacson: kung anong gagawin by our power of review and oversight, at saka yung pag-review ng National

1403
01:36:48,530 --> 01:36:49,530
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Expenditure Program.

1404
01:36:49,530 --> 01:36:51,530
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Kami na magre-review.

1405
01:36:51,530 --> 01:36:56,610
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Ang nangyari, I think it was slashed by two billion yata,

1406
01:36:56,610 --> 01:36:59,750
Senator Panfilo Lacson: o three billion eh, as proposed.

1407
01:36:59,750 --> 01:37:01,590
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So where's the fiscal autonomy?

1408
01:37:01,590 --> 01:37:06,650
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So now I'm asking the official position of the Ombudsman, if the same statutory protection

1409
01:37:06,650 --> 01:37:14,670
Senator Panfilo Lacson: sa inyong fiscal autonomy will be granted, para lang ma-enhance yung inyong integrity, independence

1410
01:37:14,670 --> 01:37:17,470
Senator Panfilo Lacson: pagdating sa budgeting process.

1411
01:37:17,470 --> 01:37:19,890
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Well, we can use that, Your Honor.

1412
01:37:19,890 --> 01:37:22,470
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It is going to be good for us if we're able to do that.

1413
01:37:22,470 --> 01:37:26,470
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But of course, we will have to be transparent about everything we do.

1414
01:37:26,470 --> 01:37:31,610
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Because it's the last moral compass that we have in government, so it has to be transparent,

1415
01:37:31,610 --> 01:37:32,610
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Your Honor.

1416
01:37:32,610 --> 01:37:33,610
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Mahirap din eh.

1417
01:37:33,610 --> 01:37:37,150
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Pag walang fiscal autonomy, at least sa implementation, sa paggastos, okay yun eh.

1418
01:37:37,150 --> 01:37:41,790
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Pero sa proposal, you're at the mercy of the DBCC.

1419
01:37:41,790 --> 01:37:47,150
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So tulad niyo, nag-propose kayo ng 12 billion plus, 12.8, something like that,

1420
01:37:47,150 --> 01:37:50,650
Senator Panfilo Lacson: pero ang cut 45% eh.

1421
01:37:50,650 --> 01:37:52,550
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So yun lang.

1422
01:37:52,550 --> 01:37:53,550
Senator Panfilo Lacson: I'm just thinking.

1423
01:37:53,550 --> 01:37:54,590
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Kasi binigyan na namin,

1424
01:37:54,590 --> 01:37:55,590
Senator Panfilo Lacson: I think,

1425
01:37:55,590 --> 01:37:56,470
Senator Panfilo Lacson: [unclear],

1426
01:38:00,470 --> 01:38:01,470
Senator Panfilo Lacson: yun ang

1427
01:38:01,470 --> 01:38:02,470
Senator Panfilo Lacson: RA number

1428
01:38:02,470 --> 01:38:03,470
Senator Panfilo Lacson: doon sa Judiciary

1429
01:38:03,470 --> 01:38:04,470
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Fiscal Autonomy

1430
01:38:04,470 --> 01:38:05,470
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Act.

1431
01:38:05,470 --> 01:38:06,470
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So ang

1432
01:38:06,470 --> 01:38:07,470
Senator Panfilo Lacson: official

1433
01:38:07,470 --> 01:38:08,470
Senator Panfilo Lacson: position ninyo is

1434
01:38:08,470 --> 01:38:09,470
Senator Panfilo Lacson: for that?

1435
01:38:09,470 --> 01:38:10,470
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yeah.

1436
01:38:10,470 --> 01:38:11,470
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

1437
01:38:11,470 --> 01:38:12,470
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes.

1438
01:38:12,470 --> 01:38:13,470
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you.

1439
01:38:13,470 --> 01:38:18,390
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Senator Lacson, actually, the Office of the Ombudsman complies itong budget, 2027,

1440
01:38:18,390 --> 01:38:25,610
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: with the requirement under Section 38 of RA 6770, which states that

1441
01:38:25,610 --> 01:38:27,610
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: the Office of the Ombudsman

1442
01:38:27,610 --> 01:38:29,930
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: shall enjoy fiscal autonomy

1443
01:38:29,930 --> 01:38:31,670
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: in its appropriations. We can just

1444
01:38:31,670 --> 01:38:33,470
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: enhance, no?

1445
01:38:33,470 --> 01:38:34,550
Senator Panfilo Lacson: That's already in the Constitution, I think

1446
01:38:34,550 --> 01:38:36,730
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Article XI?

1447
01:38:38,250 --> 01:38:38,970
Senator Panfilo Lacson: That's correct.

1448
01:38:39,350 --> 01:38:40,670
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Section 14 ba yan? Anyway,

1449
01:38:41,310 --> 01:38:43,930
Senator Panfilo Lacson: nandiyan na yun, pero ang nire-refer ko

1450
01:38:43,930 --> 01:38:44,910
Senator Panfilo Lacson: sa proposal,

1451
01:38:45,690 --> 01:38:47,650
Senator Panfilo Lacson: kasi yung fiscal autonomy nila is in

1452
01:38:47,650 --> 01:38:49,550
Senator Panfilo Lacson: the implementation, sa execution ng

1453
01:38:49,550 --> 01:38:52,150
Senator Panfilo Lacson: budget, pero hindi covered yung proposal.

1454
01:38:52,450 --> 01:38:53,650
Senator Panfilo Lacson: But then I'm wondering,

1455
01:38:53,650 --> 01:38:55,290
Senator Panfilo Lacson: meron na nga sa Judiciary,

1456
01:38:55,410 --> 01:38:57,450
Senator Panfilo Lacson: kinat pa rin ng DBCC.

1457
01:38:58,050 --> 01:38:59,670
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So where's the fiscal autonomy

1458
01:38:59,670 --> 01:39:02,250
Senator Panfilo Lacson: doon sa proposal? Dapat Congress

1459
01:39:02,250 --> 01:39:03,050
Senator Panfilo Lacson: na yung magre-review.

1460
01:39:03,650 --> 01:39:04,790
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Hindi na kayo dadaan sa

1461
01:39:04,790 --> 01:39:07,670
Senator Panfilo Lacson: budget call. You'll still be

1462
01:39:07,670 --> 01:39:09,370
Senator Panfilo Lacson: reporting to the DBCC

1463
01:39:09,370 --> 01:39:11,730
Senator Panfilo Lacson: for processing or

1464
01:39:11,730 --> 01:39:13,550
Senator Panfilo Lacson: vetting. So, anyway,

1465
01:39:13,830 --> 01:39:15,730
Senator Panfilo Lacson: May power naman yung Congress.

1466
01:39:15,730 --> 01:39:17,790
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Kami naman yung so-called power of the purse,

1467
01:39:17,890 --> 01:39:18,310
Senator Panfilo Lacson: maski hindi...

1468
01:39:20,550 --> 01:39:21,430
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Kasi hindi naman kami

1469
01:39:21,430 --> 01:39:22,230
Senator Panfilo Lacson: nag-i-implement eh.

1470
01:39:23,150 --> 01:39:23,590
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Sorry.

1471
01:39:23,650 --> 01:39:25,330
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Probably, a test would be

1472
01:39:25,330 --> 01:39:26,350
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: absorptive capacity.

1473
01:39:27,130 --> 01:39:29,510
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: The capacity to

1474
01:39:29,510 --> 01:39:31,510
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: spend the money has to be

1475
01:39:31,510 --> 01:39:33,470
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: there when we approve these

1476
01:39:33,470 --> 01:39:35,050
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: things. Because I think that's the

1477
01:39:35,050 --> 01:39:37,310
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: if I put my mind in the

1478
01:39:37,310 --> 01:39:39,010
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: myself in the seat of the executive,

1479
01:39:39,590 --> 01:39:41,330
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: it's just clearly wasting

1480
01:39:41,330 --> 01:39:43,410
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: resources if they ask for too much

1481
01:39:43,410 --> 01:39:44,850
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: and they're not able to spend it, Your Honor.

1482
01:39:48,720 --> 01:39:49,160
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Senator

1483
01:39:49,160 --> 01:39:50,720
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: President Pro Temp?

1484
01:39:51,060 --> 01:39:52,020
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Okay na, Senator Lacson?

1485
01:39:53,020 --> 01:39:54,100
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Senate President Pro Tempore,

1486
01:39:54,100 --> 01:39:55,420
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: If you're

1487
01:39:55,440 --> 01:39:58,140
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: if you're done with that topic

1488
01:39:58,140 --> 01:40:00,300
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: before, before we move

1489
01:40:00,300 --> 01:40:02,100
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: for the approval of the budget of

1490
01:40:02,100 --> 01:40:04,120
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: the Ombudsman, subject, of

1491
01:40:04,120 --> 01:40:05,460
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: course, to the amendments that are

1492
01:40:05,460 --> 01:40:06,460
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: being proposed.

1493
01:40:07,380 --> 01:40:09,120
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Just out of curiosity,

1494
01:40:11,160 --> 01:40:13,080
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: you might not be aware, but

1495
01:40:13,080 --> 01:40:14,460
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: I watch the two of you every

1496
01:40:14,460 --> 01:40:15,460
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Saturday.

1497
01:40:16,660 --> 01:40:18,540
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: And my wife

1498
01:40:18,540 --> 01:40:20,520
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: is a fan of your, what

1499
01:40:20,520 --> 01:40:22,080
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: do you call that, executive session?

1500
01:40:22,080 --> 01:40:23,100
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: No.

1501
01:40:23,100 --> 01:40:25,380
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: One time you were quoted

1502
01:40:25,440 --> 01:40:27,800
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: to say that ang tindi ng corruption

1503
01:40:27,800 --> 01:40:29,140
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: sa basura ng LGU.

1504
01:40:29,140 --> 01:40:39,820
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: How do they do that? I'm interested because

1505
01:40:39,820 --> 01:40:42,040
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: I have friends in the LGU

1506
01:40:42,040 --> 01:40:44,660
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: that are interested to find out how they

1507
01:40:45,520 --> 01:40:45,980
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: will be able to stop it.

1508
01:40:45,980 --> 01:40:47,960
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Mr. Ombudsman?

1509
01:40:47,960 --> 01:40:51,920
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: or stop it with the Ombudsman.

1510
01:40:51,920 --> 01:40:54,100
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Your Honor, may mga character tayo sa society

1511
01:40:54,100 --> 01:40:57,580
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: na basura king eh. The big haulers are basura kings, Your Honor.

1512
01:40:58,080 --> 01:41:03,400
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And they're here in Manila, in Metro Manila, in Manila, City of Manila, everywhere.

1513
01:41:04,320 --> 01:41:12,680
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And the tragedy, Your Honor, is that the work of the DENR is never started or finished

1514
01:41:12,680 --> 01:41:17,780
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: because the garbage hauling begins with local government and nothing is followed.

1515
01:41:19,280 --> 01:41:22,280
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Segregation, proper sanitary landfills.

1516
01:41:22,280 --> 01:41:25,860
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Everything becomes a dump, Your Honor.

1517
01:41:26,280 --> 01:41:26,960
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: That's the problem.

1518
01:41:28,860 --> 01:41:35,240
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But probably the DNR should have a bigger hand in it so that things will be better.

1519
01:41:35,240 --> 01:41:44,220
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: But as long as what they do is to dump the trash in specific places that they are able to contract with,

1520
01:41:46,740 --> 01:41:48,220
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: it's big money for them, Your Honor.

1521
01:41:48,700 --> 01:41:53,720
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Because the budgets for basura is so big that

1522
01:41:53,720 --> 01:41:58,580
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: it can blind a lot of people into just making money out of it.

1523
01:41:59,100 --> 01:42:02,380
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I think that for those who have been in politics for a long time,

1524
01:42:02,720 --> 01:42:03,880
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: we've seen it happen, Your Honor.

1525
01:42:04,460 --> 01:42:07,420
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: These basura kings are around the metropolis, Your Honor.

1526
01:42:08,700 --> 01:42:10,480
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: And also nationwide.

1527
01:42:11,440 --> 01:42:12,260
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Nationwide, Your Honor.

1528
01:42:14,600 --> 01:42:18,600
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: It's actually, when I started talking about this basura,

1529
01:42:19,160 --> 01:42:23,540
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: I think it touched a lot of raw nerves because we know it to be true, I think.

1530
01:42:23,720 --> 01:42:24,680
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: We know it to be true, Your Honor.

1531
01:42:25,500 --> 01:42:36,320
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: And would you have anyone in the Ombudsman that would give some local government officials

1532
01:42:36,320 --> 01:42:45,400
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: how they are going about the pattern and saan kumikita, saan natataga yung mga kababayan natin?

1533
01:42:46,200 --> 01:42:48,800
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: We will create a special investigative team for this, Your Honor.

1534
01:42:49,200 --> 01:42:49,800
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: We will do it.

1535
01:42:49,940 --> 01:42:51,960
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: All right. Thank you very much. Thank you for that.

1536
01:42:51,960 --> 01:42:52,620
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Thank you.

1537
01:42:52,620 --> 01:42:53,600
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Napag-usapan niyong basura.

1538
01:42:53,720 --> 01:42:55,880
Senator Panfilo Lacson: I was tempted to inquire about the Taguig.

1539
01:42:57,840 --> 01:43:00,700
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Baka mapagbintangan ako, nagde-demolition job.

1540
01:43:00,760 --> 01:43:07,020
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Anyway, we're quietly but surely assisting the Ombudsman in this regard,

1541
01:43:07,020 --> 01:43:09,740
Senator Panfilo Lacson: kasi I understand the complexity of the problem,

1542
01:43:10,340 --> 01:43:12,780
Senator Panfilo Lacson: yung volume ng mga graft and corruption cases.

1543
01:43:13,140 --> 01:43:15,240
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yung office nga lang namin, Mr. Ombudsman,

1544
01:43:16,100 --> 01:43:21,280
Senator Panfilo Lacson: case studies lang ang pinaggugulan namin ng panahon, pero ubos talaga oras namin.

1545
01:43:21,280 --> 01:43:23,700
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Case studies in Bulacan,

1546
01:43:23,840 --> 01:43:26,880
Senator Panfilo Lacson: case studies in Mindoro and in Taguig.

1547
01:43:27,080 --> 01:43:28,520
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Hirap na hirap na yung mga staff.

1548
01:43:28,520 --> 01:43:32,580
Senator Panfilo Lacson: What more na swarmed by so many cases ang Ombudsman,

1549
01:43:32,580 --> 01:43:38,700
Senator Panfilo Lacson: very complex, hindi lang flood control, all sorts of graft and corruption cases.

1550
01:43:39,100 --> 01:43:43,960
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So that's why we are really very supportive of the efforts of the Ombudsman

1551
01:43:44,400 --> 01:43:49,500
Senator Panfilo Lacson: and in whatever capacity na makatulong kami, like the judicial marshal service,

1552
01:43:49,920 --> 01:43:53,240
Senator Panfilo Lacson: yung fiscal autonomy, etcetera.

1553
01:43:53,240 --> 01:43:53,680
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So, he says,

1554
01:43:53,680 --> 01:44:02,100
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So rest assured that the Senate, under the leadership of the Senate President, will be foursquare behind the efforts of the Ombudsman.

1555
01:44:03,000 --> 01:44:03,600
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Thank you, Your Honor.

1556
01:44:05,480 --> 01:44:06,100
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Mr. Chairman.

1557
01:44:07,200 --> 01:44:15,680
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, before the Senate President, I would like to acknowledge also the presence of our Blue Ribbon Chair, Senator Erwin Tulfo.

1558
01:44:15,780 --> 01:44:16,780
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, sir, for joining us.

1559
01:44:16,780 --> 01:44:20,040
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Mr. Chairman, just a brief intervention lang.

1560
01:44:20,040 --> 01:44:30,360
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I was looking at itong corruption index scores natin, corruption perception index.

1561
01:44:31,200 --> 01:44:45,320
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And sad to say, in the last three years, bumagsak yung ating ranking, from 144, the lowest rank being the least corrupt.

1562
01:44:45,320 --> 01:44:49,280
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: From 144 rank naging 120 rank na tayo.

1563
01:44:50,040 --> 01:45:00,000
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And we're now the third most corrupt in Southeast Asia, next to Myanmar and Cambodia, which are...

1564
01:45:00,000 --> 01:45:02,640
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: alam naman natin, are junta states.

1565
01:45:02,920 --> 01:45:12,660
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So there is really a very big challenge for all of us to improve the perception of corruption in our country.

1566
01:45:13,160 --> 01:45:14,340
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Apektado tayo lahat eh.

1567
01:45:14,740 --> 01:45:20,180
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: In fact, one of the reasons bakit mahina ang peso, dahil walang demand sa peso.

1568
01:45:20,640 --> 01:45:22,280
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Walang nag-i-invest sa ating bansa.

1569
01:45:23,300 --> 01:45:28,900
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Kasama na dito rin itong, of course, ease of doing business and also the perception of corruption.

1570
01:45:28,900 --> 01:45:32,500
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So it's really a big challenge for all of us.

1571
01:45:33,120 --> 01:45:36,260
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And that is why I second the statement of Senator Lacson na

1572
01:45:36,580 --> 01:45:42,140
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: whatever we can do to help the Ombudsman, even the judiciary, to fight corruption, we will do it.

1573
01:45:42,820 --> 01:45:52,400
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Because it affects our country, it affects our OFWs, it affects even the most ordinary Filipino.

1574
01:45:52,860 --> 01:45:55,300
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So kailangan talaga magtulong-tulong tayo diyan.

1575
01:45:56,640 --> 01:45:57,460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, sir.

1576
01:45:58,900 --> 01:46:03,120
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Our Blue Ribbon Chair is also here.

1577
01:46:03,280 --> 01:46:04,220
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you for joining us.

1578
01:46:04,540 --> 01:46:06,580
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Senator Erwin Tulfo, you now have the floor.

1579
01:46:12,460 --> 01:46:16,240
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Anyway, I don't know, Mr. Chair, if this was already asked.

1580
01:46:16,240 --> 01:46:18,700
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Ito lang po nakita ko, napansin kanina dito.

1581
01:46:19,340 --> 01:46:22,700
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Itong total number of authorized positions, Mr. Chair.

1582
01:46:23,440 --> 01:46:28,240
Senator Erwin Tulfo: 2,439 po nire-request po ng authorized positions.

1583
01:46:28,900 --> 01:46:33,120
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Pero ang filled positions lamang ay 1,192.

1584
01:46:33,400 --> 01:46:43,040
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Dito po sa 2,439, Mr. Chair, Ombudsman, karamihan po ba nito ay mga investigators po ninyo?

1585
01:46:43,300 --> 01:46:44,580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: You would need lawyers?

1586
01:46:46,040 --> 01:46:48,100
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Sa anong mga positions po ito?

1587
01:46:48,820 --> 01:46:52,080
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: We will need more lawyers and technical investigators, Your Honor.

1588
01:46:52,420 --> 01:46:58,120
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Engineers who can educate us about infrastructure fraud, infrastructure corruption.

1589
01:46:58,900 --> 01:47:05,500
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: And other specialists, Your Honor, who are good at investigating different kinds of crimes, Your Honor.

1590
01:47:06,160 --> 01:47:08,160
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Mga normal positions po ito.

1591
01:47:08,160 --> 01:47:09,400
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I mean regular po.

1592
01:47:09,920 --> 01:47:11,500
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Regular positions po ito.

1593
01:47:11,500 --> 01:47:17,600
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Hindi po ito yung basta-bastang mga contractual employees.

1594
01:47:17,920 --> 01:47:18,200
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Your Honor.

1595
01:47:18,300 --> 01:47:19,460
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: They are plantilla positions.

1596
01:47:19,760 --> 01:47:20,220
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Plantilla positions.

1597
01:47:20,240 --> 01:47:20,620
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Yes, Your Honor.

1598
01:47:20,840 --> 01:47:21,180
Senator Erwin Tulfo: All right.

1599
01:47:21,300 --> 01:47:21,820
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Thank you po.

1600
01:47:22,200 --> 01:47:22,940
Senator Erwin Tulfo: That's all, Mr. Chair.

1601
01:47:23,640 --> 01:47:26,000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, Senator Tulfo.

1602
01:47:26,680 --> 01:47:27,040
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Likewise.

1603
01:47:27,040 --> 01:47:29,220
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Isang tanong na lang.

1604
01:47:29,340 --> 01:47:34,340
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yung tungkol sa Resident Ombudsman Program, what is the current status of the Resident Ombudsman Program,

1605
01:47:34,540 --> 01:47:39,540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: including the number of active resident ombudsmen, their deployment across agencies,

1606
01:47:39,700 --> 01:47:43,860
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and the key accomplishments or challenges encountered recently?

1607
01:47:44,320 --> 01:47:47,560
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Siguro, Assistant Ombudsman Bonoan, please.

1608
01:47:48,080 --> 01:47:54,280
Assistant Ombudsman Luis Gonzaga S. Bonoan, Jr.: Your Honor, actually, during this administration, we have reactivated the Bureau of the Resident Ombudsman,

1609
01:47:54,280 --> 01:47:55,840
Assistant Ombudsman Luis Gonzaga S. Bonoan, Jr.: which had remained inactive.

1610
01:47:55,840 --> 01:47:57,700
Assistant Ombudsman Luis Gonzaga S. Bonoan, Jr.: the last several years.

1611
01:47:58,360 --> 01:48:07,080
Assistant Ombudsman Luis Gonzaga S. Bonoan, Jr.: So, as of today, we have hired an additional 10 lawyers to complement our Bureau of Resident Ombudsman.

1612
01:48:07,280 --> 01:48:15,120
Assistant Ombudsman Luis Gonzaga S. Bonoan, Jr.: And we have plans, sir, after conducting the proper training, of fielding them out in different agencies,

1613
01:48:15,340 --> 01:48:24,820
Assistant Ombudsman Luis Gonzaga S. Bonoan, Jr.: particularly the high revenue generating agencies, sir, to investigate and collect complaints from therein.

1614
01:48:25,200 --> 01:48:25,820
Assistant Ombudsman Luis Gonzaga S. Bonoan, Jr.: Your Honor.

1615
01:48:25,840 --> 01:48:26,380
Assistant Ombudsman Luis Gonzaga S. Bonoan, Jr.: Thank you.

1616
01:48:26,800 --> 01:48:27,320
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Okay, thank you.

1617
01:48:27,840 --> 01:48:33,700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Anyway, before we close, if there are no more questions or queries from our colleagues.

1618
01:48:34,320 --> 01:48:35,840
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, Senate President Pro Tempore.

1619
01:48:36,440 --> 01:48:37,200
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

1620
01:48:37,360 --> 01:48:44,140
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: I move that we submit and approve the budget of the Ombudsman, together with the proposed amendments.

1621
01:48:44,440 --> 01:48:45,200
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I second the motion.

1622
01:48:46,080 --> 01:48:50,640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Since it has been moved by our Senate President Pro Tempore and seconded,

1623
01:48:50,640 --> 01:48:55,720
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: the budget of the Office of the Ombudsman is now deemed submitted for the plenary's consideration,

1624
01:48:55,840 --> 01:48:59,440
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: subject to the discussion and submission of documents requested.

1625
01:48:59,600 --> 01:49:05,260
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you very much, gentlemen, Ombudsman, and to all the rest of the officials of the Office of the Ombudsman.

1626
01:49:05,360 --> 01:49:05,700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you.

1627
01:49:06,080 --> 01:49:07,640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: This briefing is hereby suspended.

1628
01:49:08,280 --> 01:49:08,740
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Thank you.

1629
01:49:08,820 --> 01:49:09,280
Ombudsman Jesus Crispin C. Remulla: Thank you, sir.

